# WITH_NETW=0 overrides on top of sdkconfig.defaults (+ sdkconfig.ble when WITH_BLE=1).
#
# Empty in practice: with the network source files dropped from the CMake build
# (main/CMakeLists.txt::NETW_SRC) and the application-level WITH_NETW gates in place,
# the linker GCs all of wifi/lwip/mbedtls/esp_http_client/esp_https_ota/esp_netif/
# esp-tls/mdns/net80211/wpa_supplicant on its own. Nothing references them, so
# disabling them via Kconfig only changes build time, not the flash image.
#
# Measured: WITH_NETW=0 WITH_BLE=1 binary is ~718 KB smaller than WITH_NETW=1
# WITH_BLE=1 WITH_BINARY_TELE=1 (1,078,496 vs 1,813,392 bytes).
#
# Add disables here if a future change accidentally pulls a network component back
# into the link, or if you want to assert "this build has no networking" at the
# Kconfig level. Note: ESP_WIFI_ENABLED=n breaks arduino-esp32's WiFi.cpp compile
# (the file is unconditionally part of the arduino managed component), so the
# linker-GC path is the right default.
